<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"><head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src 'none'; script-src 'self'; script-src-attr 'none'; style-src 'self'; style-src-attr 'none'; connect-src 'none'; img-src 'none'; font-src 'none'; media-src 'none'; object-src 'none'; frame-src 'none'; worker-src 'none'; form-action 'none'; base-uri 'none'">
  <title>S149 — Five-nines evidence rehearsal</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
  <script src="model.js" defer=""></script>
  <script src="lesson.js" defer=""></script>
</head>
<body>
  <main>
    <p id="training-banner">Training rehearsal - synthetic data - not a live Azure result</p>
    <h1>S149 — Five-nines evidence</h1>
    <p>Compare counting units, inspect a fixed record, and check an expected conclusion.
      Every count, journey, event, request, user, outcome and assumption is
      <strong>fixed fictional teaching DATA ONLY</strong>. No trials, load, telemetry,
      network, cloud or user-data operations run.</p>
    <p class="notice">A correct teaching answer is not a reliability result.
      Zero observed failures is not five-nines proof. No Azure SLA or certification is claimed.</p>

    <section aria-labelledby="conduct-heading">
      <h2 id="conduct-heading">1. Select and inspect</h2>
      <form id="controls">
        <div class="choices">
          <div>
            <label for="profile-choice">Fixed fictional evidence profile</label>
            <select id="profile-choice" name="profile" disabled="">
              <option value="qualified-minimum">299,572 stipulated qualifying journeys</option>
              <option value="qualified-one-short">299,571 — exactly one trial short</option>
              <option value="request-heavy-small" selected="">6,000,000 requests; only 1,000 journeys</option>
              <option value="correlated-single-event">299,572 journeys in one correlated event</option>
              <option value="incomparable-contexts">299,572 journeys; incomparable contexts</option>
              <option value="interrupted-recovered">Four starts; original interruption then recovery</option>
              <option value="unknown-recovered">Four starts; unknown original then recovery</option>
              <option value="failure-and-unknown">Four starts; interruption and unknown retained</option>
              <option value="empty-transition-sample">Successful diagnostic requests; no journey starts</option>
            </select>
          </div>
          <div>
            <label for="count-basis">Proposed denominator unit</label>
            <select id="count-basis" name="basis" disabled="">
              <option value="REQUEST" selected="">REQUEST — diagnostic requests</option>
              <option value="USER">USER — diagnostic distinct users</option>
              <option value="EVENT">EVENT — transition clusters/contexts</option>
              <option value="JOURNEY">JOURNEY — all original attempted transition journeys</option>
            </select>
          </div>
          <div>
            <label for="expected-conclusion">Expected evidence conclusion</label>
            <select id="expected-conclusion" name="expected" disabled="">
              <option value="CONDITIONAL_BOUND_MET" selected="">Conditional illustrative bound met — not certification</option>
              <option value="INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE">Insufficient qualifying sample</option>
              <option value="ASSUMPTIONS_UNQUALIFIED">Independence or comparability unqualified</option>
              <option value="OBSERVED_INTERRUPTION">Original interruption retained</option>
              <option value="UNKNOWN_EVIDENCE">Unknown started outcome retained</option>
              <option value="NO_EVIDENCE">No attempted transition evidence</option>
              <option value="WRONG_DENOMINATOR">Wrong counting unit for the journey denominator</option>
            </select>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="actions">
          <button id="inspect-record" type="submit" disabled="">Select and inspect fixed record</button>
          <button id="check-answer" type="button" disabled="">Check teaching answer</button>
          <button id="archive-reset" type="button">Archive and reset controls</button>
        </div>
      </form>
      <p id="error" role="alert" tabindex="-1" hidden=""></p>
      <p id="attempt-mode" aria-live="polite">Retained attempt 12 of 12 — fixed record selected.</p>
      <output id="answer-status" role="status" tabindex="-1">PASS — teaching answer only; not reliability certification</output>
      <p>Native Tab / Shift+Tab, select arrows, Enter and Space work. At most twelve
        exercises are retained; reload begins a new in-memory teaching session.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="count-heading">
      <h2 id="count-heading">2. Compare counts and original outcomes</h2>
      <p id="profile-scope">One declared user journey crossing a deployment or capacity transition. Population: Four fictional original journeys; interruption and missing outcome coexist. Window: Fixed fictional original-start to declared original-budget outcome.</p>
      <p id="representation">Four fixed original outcomes; a known interruption does not erase the separate uncertainty.</p>
      <div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Counting units table">
        <table>
          <caption>Fixed fictional counts — these units are not interchangeable trials</caption>
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Unit</th><th scope="col">Count</th><th scope="col">Meaning</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody id="count-rows"><tr><th scope="row">REQUEST</th><td>80</td><td>Diagnostic requests, not independent transition trials.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">USER</th><td>4</td><td>Distinct diagnostic users, not an interchangeable trial denominator.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">EVENT</th><td>1</td><td>Transition clusters/contexts, not assumed independent comparable user journeys.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">JOURNEY</th><td>4</td><td>All original started transition journeys, including interrupted and unknown outcomes.</td></tr></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p><strong>Selected count:</strong> <output id="selected-count">4 JOURNEY — correct journey counting unit; assumptions still required</output></p>
      <p><strong>Original journey accounting:</strong> <output id="journey-counts">4 started / 2 uninterrupted / 1 interrupted / 1 unknown</output></p>
      <dl>
        <dt>Uninterrupted-transition success fraction</dt><dd><output id="success-rate">0.50000000000000000 = 2 / 4</output></dd>
        <dt>Observed interruption fraction</dt><dd><output id="interruption-rate">0.25000000000000000 = 1 / 4</output></dd>
        <dt>Unknown started-outcome fraction</dt><dd><output id="unknown-rate">0.25000000000000000 = 1 / 4</output></dd>
      </dl>
      <p>The denominator includes every started original journey. Unknown outcomes are
        not successes and cannot disappear. A later successful recovery does not repair
        the original budget or replace its outcome.</p>
      <div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Original outcomes table">
        <table>
          <caption>Original fixed outcomes (large examples use count summaries, not generated trials)</caption>
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Original ID</th><th scope="col">Outcome</th><th scope="col">Attribution</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody id="original-rows"><tr><th scope="row">J149-1</th><td>uninterrupted</td><td>Complete original fictional journey met all declared criteria.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">J149-2</th><td>interrupted</td><td>Original fictional timeout exceeded its declared journey budget.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">J149-3</th><td>uninterrupted</td><td>Complete original fictional journey met all declared criteria.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">J149-4</th><td>unknown</td><td>Original started outcome was not observed.</td></tr></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p id="recoveries">Separate later usability: J149-2 → uninterrupted; countsAsOriginalSuccess: false. Original denominator/outcome unchanged.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="confidence-heading">
      <h2 id="confidence-heading">3. Inspect uncertainty and assumptions</h2>
      <p><strong>Evidence conclusion:</strong> <output id="confidence-status">OBSERVED_INTERRUPTION</output></p>
      <p id="confidence-conclusion">Original interruption retained</p>
      <ul id="assumptions"><li>Independence: unqualified — shared dependence remains.</li><li>Comparability: stipulated for the fictional illustration, not proven.</li><li>Complete original observation: unqualified — original started outcomes remain unknown.</li><li>Aggregate counts prove assumptions: false. One shared fictional event and repeated exposure do not establish independent transition trials.</li></ul>
      <p><strong>Qualifying n assigned to this record:</strong> <output id="qualifying-n">null — no qualifying n assigned</output></p>
      <p><strong>Conditional one-sided 95% upper interruption probability:</strong>
        <output id="upper-bound">null — unqualified / unavailable, not zero</output></p>
      <p id="certification">No certification — all assumptions and counts are fictional.</p>
      <h3>Mathematical illustration only — not confidence assigned to an unqualified record</h3>
      <p><code>p_upper = -expm1(log(0.05) / n) = 1 - 0.05^(1/n)</code></p>
      <p><code>n_min = ceil(log(0.05) / log1p(-0.00001))</code></p>
      <p>With zero failures in <strong>independent, comparable, completely observed
        Bernoulli transition journeys</strong>, the smallest illustrative n is
        <output id="minimum-n">299,572</output> for an upper bound ≤ <code>0.00001</code>
        (success target ≥ <code>0.99999</code>).</p>
      <dl>
        <dt>n = 299,571 — threshold fails</dt><dd><output id="previous-upper">0.000010000024350925770 &gt; 0.00001</output></dd>
        <dt>n = 299,572 — threshold passes conditionally</dt><dd><output id="minimum-upper">0.0000099999909700545574 ≤ 0.00001 — conditional only</output></dd>
      </dl>
      <p>Requests from one user and users/transitions sharing a swap may be correlated.
        Distinct users or events alone do not establish independence, comparability or
        complete observation. This is not a universal sample-size guarantee.</p>
      <h3>Warnings and limits</h3>
      <ul id="warnings"><li>All counts and assumptions are fixed fictional teaching DATA ONLY; no trials run.</li><li>Zero observed failures is not five-nines proof.</li><li>Conditional illustration only — not a real Azure SLA, certification or confidence inferred from aggregate counts.</li><li>REQUEST, USER and EVENT are diagnostic units; all started transition JOURNEY outcomes stay in the denominator.</li><li>Retained exercises reuse fixed records, not extra independent trials; never pool them.</li><li>An original interruption remains counted after later recovery; the zero-failure bound is inapplicable.</li><li>Insufficient evidence: unknown started outcomes remain counted; complete observation is unqualified.</li><li>Insufficient evidence: correlated requests, users and transitions sharing events are not independent comparable trials.</li></ul>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="history-heading">
      <h2 id="history-heading">Retained exercise history — never pooled as new trials</h2>
      <p><strong>Session teaching verdict:</strong> <output id="session-verdict">FAIL — teaching answers only</output></p>
      <p id="history-summary">12 retained / 12 checked / 1 wrong answers / 0 unchecked. No reliability pooling or certification.</p>
      <div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Retained teaching attempts table">
        <table>
          <caption>Earlier answers, interruptions and uncertainty survive archive/reset</caption>
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Attempt</th><th scope="col">Profile / unit</th><th scope="col">Evidence</th><th scope="col">Teaching answer</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody id="history-rows"><tr><th scope="row">1</th><td>6,000,000 requests; only 1,000 journeys / REQUEST</td><td>WRONG_DENOMINATOR</td><td>FAIL — teaching only</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">2</th><td>6,000,000 requests; only 1,000 journeys / JOURNEY</td><td>INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE</td><td>PASS — teaching only</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">3</th><td>299,572 journeys in one correlated event / REQUEST</td><td>WRONG_DENOMINATOR</td><td>PASS — teaching only</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">4</th><td>299,572 journeys in one correlated event / USER</td><td>WRONG_DENOMINATOR</td><td>PASS — teaching only</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">5</th><td>299,572 journeys in one correlated event / EVENT</td><td>WRONG_DENOMINATOR</td><td>PASS — teaching only</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">6</th><td>299,572 journeys in one correlated event / JOURNEY</td><td>ASSUMPTIONS_UNQUALIFIED</td><td>PASS — teaching only</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">7</th><td>299,571 — exactly one trial short / JOURNEY</td><td>INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE</td><td>PASS — teaching only</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">8</th><td>299,572 stipulated qualifying journeys / JOURNEY</td><td>CONDITIONAL_BOUND_MET</td><td>PASS — teaching only</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">9</th><td>299,572 journeys; incomparable contexts / JOURNEY</td><td>ASSUMPTIONS_UNQUALIFIED</td><td>PASS — teaching only</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">10</th><td>Four starts; unknown original then recovery / JOURNEY</td><td>UNKNOWN_EVIDENCE</td><td>PASS — teaching only</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">11</th><td>Four starts; original interruption then recovery / JOURNEY</td><td>OBSERVED_INTERRUPTION</td><td>PASS — teaching only</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">12</th><td>Four starts; interruption and unknown retained / JOURNEY</td><td>OBSERVED_INTERRUPTION</td><td>PASS — teaching only</td></tr></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
